      "id": "promote",
      "label": "Promote a change",
      "state": "not-run-for-this-entry",
      "summary": "No promotion is recorded for this entry.",
      "basis": [
        "lifecycle.promotion"
      ],
      "commands": [
        {
          "comment": "preview what the dev variant would take from the base",
          "command": "cub variant promote <your-space>-dev --dry-run -o mutations",
          "needsAccount": true
        },
        {
          "comment": "promote once you have read the preview",
          "command": "cub variant promote <your-space>-dev --change-desc \"Pull the reviewed base forward\"",
          "needsAccount": true,
          "writes": true
        },
        {
          "comment": "delete the installer record that the promotion adds back",
          "command": "cub unit delete --space <your-space>-dev installer-record",
          "needsAccount": true,
          "writes": true
        },
        {
          "comment": "publish the Release that carries the change",
          "command": "cub release publish <your-space>-dev",
          "needsAccount": true,
          "writes": true
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "The promotion changes the dev Space and publishes nothing. It also adds the `installer-record` Unit back with the Target. The change reaches the cluster only after the delete and the publish.",
        "The preview lists the whole installer record as added. In the walk, the preview of a one-label change to gpu-operator ran to 405 lines, and about 400 of them were that record."
      ],
